{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794126338,"nonce":"TIT2OwHXkAw/enmVsUlkA0uo86E=","title":"Book theming chapter predates :root support and teaches only Rust token reads","message":"The Theming chapter was written before CSS had :root variables, var() against theme tokens, component layers and per-component --cn-* hooks. It teaches reading ThemeState in Rust and passing colours to builders, and never says that every token is a :root variable an app can override. That gap produced GitHub issue 68 (asking for colour setters on the cn textarea, which the theme and CSS already cover).\n\nAlso stale in the chapter: the \"Default Theme: Catppuccin\" section (BlincTheme is now an alias of HybridTheme; Restrained and Expressive are not mentioned), the Linux detection row (GTK_THEME and gsettings only, the XDG portal is not queried), and the custom-theme example (no optional shape()).\n\nScope: add the CSS-variable workflow (token names, :root precedence, scoped --cn-* hooks, per-scheme CSS via set_css, CSS first and Rust reads for custom paint), replace the Catppuccin section with the built-in themes, correct the detection row, link the CSS Styling chapter instead of repeating its token tables.","files":null}]}